Findings:

- **check CANNOT FAIL / STATUS CODE REPORTING WRAPPER**: line 125.  
  Exact input: a repo containing `BAD_REVIEW.html` with `<html><body></body></html>`, then run `python scripts/fix_review_title_template.py`.  
  Consequence: `NO_PAGE_TITLE` is counted, but `main()` returns `None`, so the process exits `0` and any gate sees success.

- **probe keyed to the STRING A FIX REMOVES**: line 77.  
  Exact input: `<title>RapidMeta Cardiology | Correct Trial v1.0</title><tr><td class="p-4 w-1/4 font-bold text-slate-400">Review Title</td><td class="p-4 text-slate-300">Wrong Trial Title</td></tr>`.  
  Consequence: the mismatch is real, but because the old value lacks one of four hardcoded strings, line 80 returns `BESPOKE_KEEP` and the defect persists.

- **SELECTOR KEYED TO A FORM THE CORPUS MAY NOT USE**: line 33.  
  Exact input: `<title>RapidMeta Cardiology | Correct v1.0</title><tr>\n<td class="p-4 w-1/4 font-bold text-slate-400">Review Title</td><td class="p-4 text-slate-300">Network Meta-Analysis of Sodium-Glucose Co-transporter-2 Inhibitors</td></tr>`.  
  Consequence: a semantically identical row with whitespace after `<tr>` is reported as `NO_REVIEW_TITLE_ROW`, so it is never patched.

- **values compared/written AS TEXT where line endings differ**: line 107.  
  Exact input: an LF-only `X_REVIEW.html` matching the known-wrong template path, run on Windows without `--dry-run`.  
  Consequence: `read_text()` normalizes newlines and `write_text()` writes platform newlines, so the patch can rewrite unrelated line endings across the file.

No finding: idempotency guard satisfied by its own comment or marker.

COULD NOT DETERMINE: instrument reading a different copy; missing expected caller/invocation contract.

No finding: merged-cell or off-by-one tabulation/count.

No finding: zero conflated with absent.

No finding: negation dropped.
